%description:
Tests icmpSequenceCheck, the rule of Linux (tcp_v4_err()) that RFC 5927 section
4.1 describes. The tester answers the SYN of the client with Protocol
Unreachable (3/2), a hard error, but its quoted segment carries sequence number
100000, outside SND.UNA to SND.MAX (0 to 1). The client ignores the error as
stale and opens the connection with its next SYN.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

sim-time-limit = 10s
*.cli_tcp.icmpSequenceCheck = true
*.tcptester.script="A1 icmp 3 2 100000"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.001 A001] A.1000 > B.2000: S 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# answering with an ICMP error
[3.001 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: S 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
srv_tcp: LISTEN --> SYN_RCVD  (on RCV_SYN)
[3.003 B001] A.1000 < B.2000: A S 750500:750500(0) ack 1 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
[3.005 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A ack 750501 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
Ignoring the ICMP error: it quotes sequence number 100000, outside SND.UNA=0 to SND.MAX=1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
